  "scope": {
    "implementedInternalRead": "GET /internal/v1/migration/company-research-parity/{ticker}",
    "behavior": [
      "Spring loads the current company quote directly from Yahoo chart metadata instead of using the legacy company projection as its normalization input",
      "query1 then query2 fallback, range=5d, interval=1d, UTC market date, and the MMC-to-MRSH compatibility symbol preserve the Node collector contract",
      "Yahoo JSON, HTTP, retry, and cache types remain in the outbound adapter; application receives only a framework-free quote projection and domain receives only the numeric price",
      "the response exposes quoteMatched and legacy/Spring quote values before comparing fundamentals, Company Score, and Buy Score",
      "successful quotes are bounded to 128 tickers, fresh for one minute, stale for at most fifteen minutes, and protected by per-ticker single-flight",
      "different external quote fetches are limited to eight concurrent operations and malformed or failed responses never replace the last successful quote",
      "the endpoint remains demand-driven and adds no startup fetch, persistence write, scheduler, notification, or Telegram side effect"
    ],
    "remainingInNode": [
      "analyst consensus collection and history persistence used by market expectations",
      "Yahoo price history used by bottom and reversal signals",
